  "prefLabel": "Env-A 1204.36 Stencil coating",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 1204.36 \"Stencil coating\" means an ink or pigmented coating that is rolled or brushed onto a template or stamp at a thickness of not more than one mil of coating solids, typically used to form letters, numbers, or decorative designs.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-A 1200) #9933, eff 6-1-11; ss by #12899, eff 10-17-19",
